{"name":"Steampunk","deep":true,"image":{"url":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2b/Steampunk-falksen.jpg/960px-Steampunk-falksen.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail","credit":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Steampunk-falksen.jpg","caption":"Steampunk-falksen","source":"Wikimedia Commons"},"mentions":0,"casual":{"lead":["Steampunk is a science-fiction subgenre and aesthetic built on 19th-century steam-era machinery, and steampunk fashion is its look: Victorian-style garments mixed with brass goggles, gears and rugged or post-apocalyptic touches. People use it as a costume or lifestyle style to present a distinctive, handmade appearance.","The style grew from late-20th-century novels and spread through conventions, Etsy craft sellers and runway collections. It is a style choice, so its payoff is in presentation and personal identity rather than any measured physical change."],"sections":[{"h":"How people use it","paras":["Followers assemble outfits from corsets and waistcoats, long coats, bustled or bell skirts, top hats or bowlers, boots, pocket watches and goggles, often handmade or modified. Hair, makeup and jewelry are styled to match, and events and conventions are where full outfits are worn."],"subs":[]},{"h":"Risks & side effects","paras":["Steampunk is a low-risk style. Corsets worn tightly can be uncomfortable, and costume pieces such as heavy leather, brass and buckles are practical considerations for heat and movement."],"subs":[]}]},"gallery":[{"url":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2b/Steampunk-falksen.jpg/960px-Steampunk-falksen.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail","full":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/2/2b/Steampunk-falksen.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=original","title":"Steampunk-falksen","license":"CC BY-SA 3.0","creator":"Tyrus Flynn","page":"https