EVEN","url":"https://t-nation.com/t/geek-s-t-seven/170955","site":"T Nation · 1127 posts · 2011"},{"title":"Geek S**T 8.061","url":"https://t-nation.com/t/geek-s-t-8-061/175164","site":"T Nation · 1126 posts · 2012"},{"title":"Geek S**T Generation FOUR.ZERO","url":"https://t-nation.com/t/geek-s-t-generation-four-zero/150771","site":"T Nation · 1126 posts · 2010"},{"title":"Fat Bottom Girls","url":"https://t-nation.com/t/fat-bottom-girls/170110","site":"T Nation · 1126 posts · 2011"},{"title":"More Movies You've Watched This Week","url":"https://t-nation.com/t/more-movies-youve-watched-this-week/129780","site":"T Nation · 1124 posts · 2009"},{"title":"(de)Motivational Posters, Random Pics 4.0","url":"https://t-nation.com/t/de-motivational-posters-random-pics-4-0/152930","site":"T Nation · 1120 posts · 2010"},{"title":"Geek S**T 3 Gen","url":"https://t-nation.com/t/geek-s-t-3-gen/129779","site":"T Nation · 1020 posts · 2009"},{"title":"Drinker with a Gym Problem","url":"https://t-nation.com/t/drinker-with-a-gym-problem/138280","site":"T Nation · 961 posts · 2009"},{"title":"I Don't Warm Up, I Don't Stretch","url":"https://t-nation.com/t/i-dont-warm-up-i-dont-stretch/240386","site":"T Nation · 791 posts · 2018"},{"title":"Even Breathing Feels All Right","url":"https://t-nation.com/t/even-breathing-feels-all-right/159117","site":"T Nation · 504 posts · 2011"},{"title":"Planet Fitness Transgender Policy","url":"https://t-nation.com/t/planet-fitness-transgender-policy/287277","site":"T Nation · 241 posts · 2024"},{"title":"Stupid Stuff I Do for Attention","url":"https://t-nation.com/t/stupid-stuff-i-do-for-attention/278817","site":"T Nation · 217 posts · 2022"}],"news":[],"social":[],"web":[{"title":"Steampunk — Grokipedia","url":"https://grokipedia.com/page/Steampunk"},{"title":"Steampunk (Wikipedia)","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Steampunk"},{"title":"Steampunk fashion (Wikipedia)","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Steampunk_fashion"}]},"angle":{"goal":"Style & presentation","chain":["Choose Victorian-industrial clothing and accessories","Build a coordinated, distinctive outfit","A memorable personal look"],"effect":"direct","text":"Steampunk is a clothing and styling choice. Wearers use corsets, vests, hats, goggles and themed hair and makeup to present a distinctive aesthetic."},"wikipedia":null,"grokipedia":"https://grokipedia.com/page/Steampunk","lead":["Steampunk is a science-fiction subgenre featuring retro-futuristic technology inspired by 19th-century steam-powered machinery, usually set in alternate Victorian or Edwardian worlds [1]. As an aesthetic subculture it covers art, clothing and performance in that style [1].","Steampunk fashion is its wearable form. It blends a romanticised Victorian view of science with 19th-century industrial elements and spans clothing, hairstyling, jewelry, body modification and makeup [2]. Typical pieces include corsets worn as outerwear, waistcoats, lab coats, long skirts with bustles, brass goggles, hats such as bowlers and pith helmets, and mechanical-looking jewelry [2].","People adopt the style to stand out and to look distinctive and handmade. The look has no fixed rules [1], and its influence has reached the runway: Christian Dior's John Galliano brought steampunk elements to a 2010 show [2]."],"infobox":[["Type","Fashion subculture / aesthetic"],["Origin","Late-20th-century science fiction; term coined by K. W. Jeter in 1987"],["Signature items","Corsets, waistcoats, brass goggles, top hats"],["First steampunk clothing company","Steampunk Couture (Kate Lambert, 2005)"],["First convention","SalonCon (2006)"]],"sections":[{"h":"Origins and spread","paras":["In a 1987 letter to Locus magazine, author K. W. Jeter suggested the name steampunk for a group of 19th-century-set novels by himself, Tim Powers and James Blaylock, as a counterpart to cyberpunk [1]. The label was applied retroactively to earlier works such as Jeter's Morlock Night (1979), which is also considered the first steampunk novel and the starting point of the fashion [1][2].","Steampunk grew alongside goth and punk scenes in the 1980s and 1990s [2]. In 2005 Kate Lambert founded Steampunk Couture, reportedly the first steampunk clothing company, and the first steampunk convention, SalonCon, followed in 2006 [2]. Between 2009 and 2011 the term became a common label for handmade goods on Etsy [1]. The Oxford Museum of the History of Science hosted the first major steampunk art exhibition in 2009 to 2010, with over 80,000 visitors [1]."],"subs":[]},{"h":"Description","paras":["Steampunk dress has no fixed rules and mixes Victorian pieces such as corsets, bustles, waistcoats and top hats with military or post-apocalyptic elements such as gas masks [1]. Brass goggles are the signature accessory [2]. Modern versions can be as casual as graphic tees or jeans with belts and holsters [2].","The aesthetic has strong ties to DIY craft, and enthusiasts modify modern objects with brass, wood and leather to give them a Victorian appearance [1]."],"subs":[]},{"h":"In fashion and media","paras":["Steampunk appears in film, television, photography and music, and in 2012 an episode of America's Next Top Model featured a steampunk-themed shoot [2]. The style began influencing mainstream fashion trends from about 2015 [2]."],"subs":[]},{"h":"Clinical studies","paras":["No studies found."],"subs":[]}],"lore":null,"timeline":[{"year":"1979","event":"K. W. Jeter's Morlock Night published, considered the first steampunk novel [2]."},{"year":"1987","event":"Jeter proposes the term steampunk in a letter to Locus [1]."},{"year":"2005","event":"Steampunk Couture founded by Kate Lambert [2]."},{"year":"2006","event":"SalonCon, the first steampunk convention [2]."},{"year":"2009","event":"First major steampunk art exhibition opens at the Oxford Museum of the History of Science [1]."},{"year":"2010","event":"Steampunk elements appear in a John Galliano collection for Dior [2]."}],"refs":[{"title":"Steampunk","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Steampunk","source":"Wikipedia","year":2025,"type":"encyclopedia"},{"title":"Steampunk fashion","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Steampunk_fashion","source":"Wikipedia","year":2025,"type":"encyclopedia"}],"studies":[],"reddit":[],"forums":[{"title":"Flame Free Confession III: Even More Flame Free (Part 2)","url":"https://t-nation.com/t/flame-free-confession-iii-even-more-flame-free-part-2/273731","site":"T Nation · 8490 posts · 2021"},{"title":"Trump: The Second Year","url":"https://t-nation.com/t/trump-the-second-year/237562","site":"T Nation · 2551 posts · 2018"},{"title":"No Promises This Time","url":"https://t-nation.com/t/no-promises-this-time/268158","site":"T Nation · 1527 posts · 2020"},{"title":"Geek S**T SEVEN","url":"https://t-nation.com/t/geek-s-t-seven/170955","site":"T Nation · 1127 posts · 2011"},{"title":"Geek S**T 8.061","url":"https://t-nation.com/t/geek-s-t-8-061/175164","site":"T Nation · 1126 posts · 2012"},{"title":"Geek S**T Generation FOUR.ZERO","url":"https://t-nation.com/t/geek-s-t-generation-four-zero/150771","site":"T Nation · 1126 posts · 2010"}]}